    {
      "id": "claim_5712564d44244197a155ef4bdc054f9f",
      "statement": "Each picked file gets a fresh AES-256-GCM key that is exported raw and RSA-wrapped with the receiver's public key — and a pick made while encryption is on but the peer's rsaPub has not been imported yet (the offer is still pending) is rejected with an error toast instead of being registered with an empty wrapped key. The wrapped key bytes travel in MetaData.key and the receiver unwraps them with its private key in onMetaData, keeping the result on the file detail for chunk decryption; the receiver registers the file entry at WaitingAccept BEFORE the async key decryption, and on unwrap failure sets a visible error on the entry, toasts, sends EVENT_VALIDATE_ERROR to the sender, and returns without accepting. A metadata-failed entry (error set, or missing aesKey on an encrypted session) additionally cannot be force-accepted: Receiver.onAccept guards its entry point and refuses such entries with a toast plus EVENT_RECEIVER_REJECT instead of starting a transfer that can never succeed (PR #78). Pick-time crypto failures are equally visible: onFilesPick iterates with an async for...of (not a fire-and-forget forEach) so a generateAesKey/encryptAesKeyWithRsaPublicKey rejection toasts and skips the entry instead of escaping as an unhandled rejection (PR #75).",
      "evidence": [
