    {
      "id": "claim_c5d863ce334a49c989924000c2fb6a3c",
      "statement": "Failure behavior is degraded-not-crashing: a missing per-file aesKey makes the sender fall back to sending that chunk plaintext, a malformed 'p' param downgrades isEncrypt to false with an error toast (the answer no longer advertises encryption), a damaged non-empty answer-code key or missing separator aborts acceptance with an error toast, a well-formed answer code with an empty key portion is the receiver's deliberate plaintext downgrade and the offer side follows it into plaintext (effectiveEncrypt=false, info toast) instead of dead-ending the handshake, a file picked before the answer is accepted is rejected with a visible error instead of being registered with an undeliverable empty key, a pick whose key-encryption crypto call rejects is skipped with a visible error (PR #75), and encryption off means no keys are generated and all chunks are sent without crypto.",
