    {
      "id": "claim_85040d6ca22c4a45981a13d163065e72",
      "statement": "tests/crypto.test.mjs is one of the regression guards `npm test` runs via `node --no-warnings --test \\\"tests/*.test.mjs\\\"`; it asserts the RSA-OAEP modulusLength constant in src/utils/crypto.ts is 2048 and that a freshly generated RSA public key exports as a 2048-bit modulus, so any future silent revert of the constant to 1024 fails the test. It also pins the OAEP digest regression (PR #73): no bare-name RSA-OAEP option object may survive (static regex), both encrypt and decrypt call sites must pin `hash: rsaGenParams.hash` (SHA-256, the keygen digest), and a runtime round-trip of an AES-256 key through encryptAesKeyWithRsaPublicKey/decryptAesKeyWithRsaPrivateKey must come back byte-identical.",
      "evidence": [
