    {
      "id": "claim_22ae504e43e447edb1467001c15014f4",
      "statement": "Receiver key-unwrap failure is visible, not silent, and it signals the sender: if decryptAesKeyWithRsaPrivateKey rejects for an incoming file, the already-registered entry gets an error set, an error toast fires, and onMetaData sends EVENT_VALIDATE_ERROR back to the sender (bouncing its file to Pending) before returning without accepting. The metadata-failed entry stays in WaitingAccept with the error shown (FileCard error banner) and is not a Remove-only dead-end (PR #76) — but Accept on it is refused (PR #78): onAccept checks the entry's error/aesKey state up front, toasts 'Cannot accept <name>: the metadata/key failed to process — the sender must resend the file', and sends EVENT_RECEIVER_REJECT instead of EVENT_RECEIVER_ACCEPT, so the entry stays in WaitingAccept with Deny/Remove as the real exits.",
